Shaper Insight is a companion to the OPNsense traffic shaper (Firewall: Shaper:
Shaper Insight). It is not related to Reporting: Insight (NetFlow).
Earlier name: os-shaper-assistant.

It shows whether the shaper really does what its configuration says:
which scheduler each pipe runs in the kernel (CAKE through the os-cake
plugin, or FQ-CoDel), the configuration against what is loaded, settings
that the chosen scheduler ignores, per-tin CAKE statistics, health checks,
and the compiled configuration in a form that can be pasted into a forum
post with public addresses, host names and descriptions redacted.

When you ask it to, it also changes the configuration:
- Apply writes shaper pipes, queues and rules (and os-cake entries) for
  your internet links, after showing the exact plan, with a 60 second
  confirm timer that puts the previous shaper settings back. You can let
  it disable your own conflicting shaper rules.
- Remove deletes what it created and switches those rules back on.
- Priorities load ipfw rules that mark chosen devices, aliases or ports
  for a CAKE class.
- A history sampler (on by default, off in the settings) reads the pipe
  and pf state counters every 10 seconds and keeps fixed-size RRD files
  in /var/db/rrd (shown in Reporting: Health under "shaper") plus a
  6 hour per-device file in /var/run. The files stay after uninstall.
- The bufferbloat test sends traffic to third-party servers you choose.

To take its shaping away, press Remove before uninstalling: uninstalling
alone leaves your shaper as it is (priorities turn off), and a reinstall
picks the setup up again.
os-cake is optional: it is detected at runtime.

Plugin Changelog
================

1.0.h

* "Limiting now" needs the pipe near its cap in 2 of the last 3
  steps, or drops at half the cap or more; a stray drop is not
  limiting
* "Background is using the free line" only when the other classes
  carry next to nothing (2 % of the line); near its 1/16 floor
  while the others fill the line it says "yielding"
* CAKE tins drawn with fixed textures, so host colours mean hosts
  only; sort arrows no longer cover right-aligned headers

1.0.g

* Sharing: per-host rates scaled to what the pipe sent (pf counts
  packets before the shaper drops them), with the offered rate shown
* Sampler survives config saves (locked, retried reads), has a
  watchdog (cron, 5 min) and a health check, caps the pf state read
  (paused above 50,000 states, slower when costly) and gives memory
  back after a state flood
* Pipe history no longer waits for pf; readings judged by the cap of
  their time; "Background is yielding" and the 1/16 floor per pipe
* A package change or removal stops a running sampler
* Upgrading in place keeps loaded priority marks and their counters
* Every table sorts (click or keyboard; addresses by value), shows
  an empty state and fits a phone; host tables show Name, IP, MAC
  and Manufacturer (core's IEEE list), shared and random MACs
* Sharing: at most 8 coloured hosts with stable colours, the rest
  one band; legend above the chart; "Find a host"; the other hosts
  listed on demand from the newest step, windowed beyond 100 rows
* Alias, pipe, queue and interface names link to their core page
  with the content on hover

1.0.f

* Sharing page: per-device rates under each pipe's payload cap, CAKE
  drops, marks and delay, per-class rates with the Bulk threshold
* History sampler with RRD files (10 s for 6 h up to 1 h for a year)
* Priorities by port (udp/51820, tcp+udp/6881-6889); a warning when one
  MAC has several addresses (containers sharing the host's MAC)
* Live rates stamped at the counter read; points above the cap flagged
* Every scheduler name shown (WF2Q+, QFQ, FIFO, FQ-PIE, DRR, PRIO) has a
  glossary entry, and each pipe says why it runs its scheduler

1.0.d

* Renamed from os-shaper-assistant; on install, its settings, ledger,
  restore points and bufferbloat results are moved over once (logged)
* Objects made under the old name stay the plugin's own; the next Apply
  renames them in place
* Mutating configd actions limited to wheel and wwwonly
